<%#
  The interactive Measure view — .lbrn/.lbrn2, .mage, .dxf, .svg. See measure_controller.js.

  Mirrors the 3D viewer's lazy pattern: nothing is fetched until the user clicks Measure, which
  matters because the payload reaches 281 KB gzipped on the densest real files and most pages are
  never measured.

  ONE PARTIAL FOR ALL FOUR FORMATS, with only the POSTER differing (below). The controller is
  format-agnostic — it reads a wire contract, not a file type — so a per-format partial would be
  four copies of one surface differing in a single <img>, which is the shape §14d's five
  `port_writable?` copies warn about.
%>
<div class="measure-view"
     data-controller="measure"
     data-measure-url-value="<%= geometry_file_path(@node.node_id) %>"
     data-measure-name-value="<%= @node.name %>">
  <div class="measure-stage" data-measure-target="stage"></div>
  <div class="measure-bar">
    <span class="measure-dims" data-measure-target="dims"></span>
    <span class="measure-launch">
      <button type="button" class="btn small" data-action="measure#load">Measure</button>
    </span>
    <span class="measure-actions">
      <%#
        THE PAPER OPTIONS ARE POPULATED BY THE CONTROLLER FROM print_sheet.js's PAPERS table, not
        listed here. A second copy of the paper list in ERB is a second definition that drifts, and
        this select only ever appears once the controller has run anyway.
      %>
      <button type="button" class="btn small ghost" data-action="measure#toggleSelect"
              data-measure-target="selectToggle" aria-pressed="false">Select parts</button>
      <select class="measure-paper" aria-label="Paper size"
              data-measure-target="paper" data-action="measure#paperChanged"></select>
      <button type="button" class="btn small" data-action="measure#print"
              data-measure-target="printButton">Print all</button>
      <%#
        VISIBLE TEXT IS CONSTANT, THE ACCESSIBLE NAME IS NOT. The bar already carries five other
        controls, so a second count-bearing label beside "Print 3 parts" is noise — but the button
        must still say what it will do, so refreshPrintBar() writes aria-label/title from the same
        targetNoun() the Print label uses. The literals here are the at-rest state the controller
        writes on draw(); they must agree with it, exactly as "Print all" does above.
      %>
      <button type="button" class="btn small ghost" data-action="measure#downloadSvg"
              data-measure-target="svgButton"
              aria-label="Download all as SVG" title="Download all as SVG">SVG</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn small ghost" data-action="measure#reset">Reset</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn small ghost" aria-label="Return to image"
              data-action="measure#showPoster">✕ Image</button>
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="measure-fallback" data-measure-target="fallback">
    <%#
      THE POSTER: what the page shows at rest, before Measure is clicked, and what ✕ Image
      returns to.

      AN SVG IS ITS OWN POSTER — served from the blob endpoint into an <img>, exactly as the
      :image branch does. That is NOT a relaxation of the rule that this app never inlines user
      SVG (§15): an <img> src is a replaced element, so scripts in the document do not run and it
      cannot reach this page's DOM. Inlining the markup is what is forbidden, and nothing here
      does that — the Measure drawing itself is built from parsed coordinates, never from the
      file's own markup.

      Every other format posts its server-rendered thumbnail, reproducing ALL THREE states the
      :thumbnail branch handles, because these extensions no longer reach it.
    %>
    <% if File.extname(@node.name).downcase == ".svg" %>
      <img src="<%= blob_file_path(@node.node_id) %>" alt="<%= @node.name %>" class="preview-image">
    <% elsif @thumbnail&.status == "ready" && @thumbnail.asset.attached? %>
      <img src="<%= url_for(@thumbnail.asset) %>" alt="Preview of <%= @node.name %>" class="preview-image">
    <% elsif %w[pending processing].include?(@thumbnail&.status) %>
      <p class="muted">Generating preview…</p>
    <% else %>
      <p class="muted">No inline preview for this file.</p>
      <%= link_to "Download #{@node.name}", blob_file_path(@node.node_id, download: 1), class: "btn" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
